From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:53:52 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: Use macOS's watchdog thresholds

Region C +0x24, +0x9c8, +0x9cc and +0x9d0 are the firmware watchdog's
relaxed and ordinary thresholds, its recovery escalation threshold and
its channel-mask intervention threshold, all counted in checks of
unchanged work (about one a millisecond). The driver had 4096, 64, 64
and 2; macOS 26.6.2 sets 3000, 40, 50 and 1 on the J713 (captured by
Niklas Sheth). The meanings are from interface notes by Syd Garlathy
<s@ll.dev>, written from macOS's drivers.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_platform.rs | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_platform.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_platform.rs
index ee15df758144..a871d9812eac 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_platform.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_platform.rs
@@ -414,14 +414,16 @@ pub(crate) fn region_c(&self) -> Result<KVec<u8>> {
             (0x7f0, 1),
             (0xe28, crate::module_parameters::fault_control.value()),
             (0xe2c, 1),
-            (0x24, 4096),
             (0x998, 32),
             (0x99c, 8),
             (0x9a0, 256),
             (0x9a4, 1),
-            (0x9c8, 64),
-            (0x9cc, 64),
-            (0x9d0, 2),
+            // Watchdog thresholds, in checks of unchanged work: relaxed,
+            // ordinary, recovery escalation and channel-mask intervention.
+            (0x24, 3000),
+            (0x9c8, 40),
+            (0x9cc, 50),
+            (0x9d0, 1),
             (0x84, self.maximum_power),
             (0x88, top_state),
             (0x8c, top_state),
